the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$, \nfind a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=-2{x}_{3},$ where ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112115/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fd5a675-c692-505e-900b-d7500fb7c653"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
